  "worked_solution": "First, we find the reference angle associated with the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061|\\frac{-4}{4}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}\u20611 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the ray lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we find the angle in the fourth quadrant that has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =2\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar equation of the ray is \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.\n$$",
